-- title:
--   Index p-1 of ±Γ₁(Mp) in ±(Γ₁(M)∩Γ₀(p))
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $3 \le M$ and let $p$ be a prime natural number with $p \nmid M$. Inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, with $\Gamma_1(N)$ and $\Gamma_0(N)$ the standard congruence subgroups and $\langle -1\rangle =$ `Subgroup.zpowers (-1 : SL(2, ℤ))` the subgroup of integer powers of $-1$, four assertions hold simultaneously. First, $\Gamma_1(Mp) \le \Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)$. Second, the translation matrix `ModularGroup.T`, that is $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$, lies in $\Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)$. Third, every element $\gamma$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)$ together with $-1$ satisfies $\gamma \in \Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)$ or $-\gamma \in \Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)$. Fourth, the relative index, in Mathlib's sense, of $\Gamma_1(Mp) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ in $(\Gamma_1(M) \sqcap \Gamma_0(p)) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ equals $p - 1$ (a truncated subtraction of natural numbers); since the former group is contained in the latter by the first assertion, this is the ordinary index $[\pm(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)) : \pm\Gamma_1(Mp)]$.
--
--   This is the standard index computation for congruence subgroups: reduction of the lower-right entry modulo $p$ identifies $(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))/\Gamma_1(Mp)$ with $(\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})^\times$, the group of diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})^\times$, and the hypothesis $M \ge 3$ ensures $-1 \notin \Gamma_1(M)$ so that adjoining $\pm 1$ does not change the index. It is used to compute the degree of the extension of function fields of the modular curves $X_1(Mp)$ and $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$, in [`ModularCurve.relfinrank_eq_sub_one_x1FunctionField_mul_x1x0`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_eq_sub_one_x1FunctionField_mul_x1x0); the auxiliary first three conjuncts supply the inclusion, an element of infinite order, and the $\pm$ decomposition needed there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_relIndex_gamma1_mul_sup_zpowers_neg_one_gamma1_inf_gamma0_eq_sub_one.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
